    "result_text": "All 3 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## What I changed\n\nI agreed with the finding \u2014 the city\u2192region table was duplicated and the codebase already has the shared-helper idiom (`OwnerAddress`). I extracted it:\n\n- **New `OwnerLocality`** (alongside `OwnerAddress` in `function/owner/`) \u2014 the single source of truth for the city\u2192region table, exposing `regionFor(String city)` which returns the canonical region or `null` for a city with no known region. It's `public` because `OwnerMapper` lives in a different package.\n- **`ValidateOwnerPostcode`** now calls `OwnerLocality.regionFor(...)` instead of its own private `CITY_REGION` copy. The postcode-range table stays local to the validator, as suggested (the mapper doesn't need it). The `null`-means-no-region contract maps cleanly onto its existing \"no range \u2192 accept any 4-digit\" logic, so no behaviour changed.\n- **`OwnerMapper.locality`** now derives from the same helper, mapping the shared `null` contract to its display sentinel (`\"UNKNOWN\"`), keeping the read-time output identical.\n\nThe two sides of the rule now share one table, so a future city addition is a one-line change in one place.",
